    {
      "id": "hierarchy",
      "version": "1.0.0",
      "title": "Hierarchy Rollup",
      "description": "Roll a tree up to totals: charts of accounts, cost centres, bills of materials, org units. Over relation(Child, child_of, Parent) and metric(Node, amount, Value) facts, hier_subtotal/2 gives a node's own amount plus every descendant's at any depth, hier_subtotals/1 gives every node at once, and why/2 shows the facts behind a total. The closure is a bottom-up fixpoint, so loops in the data terminate, are reported by hier_cycle/1 and never double-count; hier_problems/1 flags loops, double parents and non-numeric amounts. Any metric name via the /3 forms. Pure ISO; runs on SWI and Scryer.",
